      PracticeQuestion(
        scenario:
            "Question 8: (a) Mention four reasons why money should be kept out of children's reach.\n"
            "(b) In what four ways do people misuse money in your community?\n"
            "(BECE 2009 Q8)",
        answer: "Correct Answer: (a) Answer:\n"
            "⦿ Risk of physical destruction — Young children lack an understanding of financial value and can easily shred paper currency into pieces.\n"
            "⦿ Soiling and defacing currency — Handling notes with dirty, food-stained, or muddy hands heavily defaces and degrades state-printed money.\n"
            "⦿ Rejection due to crumpling — Shoving currency roughly into tight spaces wrinkles it badly, which can cause traders to reject it.\n"
            "⦿ Moisture damage — Wet or sweat-stained hands weaken the fiber of paper currency, speeding up tearing.\n"
            "⦿ Ruining coin layouts — Children might punch holes or scratch coins, ruining the official legal metallic layout.\n"
            "⦿ Premature exposure and peer pressure — Easy access to cash can lead children to buy unhealthy treats and expose them to negative peer manipulation.\n"
            "⦿ Cultivating bad habits — Unmonitored contact with money can tempt children to pilfer cash from parents without consent.\n"
            "⦿ Severe health and choking hazards — Children often place items in their mouths, presenting risks of swallowing coins or contracting bacterial infections from germs on cash.\n"
            "⦿ Skin conditions — Placing dirty cash against sensitive skin or inside undergarments can introduce bacteria, leading to rashes and itching.\n"
            "⦿ High printing costs for the state — Damaging circulating currency forces the government to divert massive public funds toward printing replacements.\n\n"
            "Answer: (b)\n"
            "⦿ Gambling and excessive betting — Risking essential family resources on lotteries, sports betting, and highly volatile raffles.\n"
            "⦿ Funding criminal activities — Spending money to bribe judicial settings, acquire illicit weapons, or facilitate theft and robbery.\n"
            "⦿ Frivolous and unhealthy spending — Diverting household savings toward addictive habits like smoking cigarettes or lavish entertainment.\n"
            "⦿ Unplanned, careless giving — Squandering money on unnecessary items without long-term family investment planning.",
        explanation: ".",
